      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I would say no, as Legacy is not actually being dealt damage. On the other hand, if Legacy would be dealt 1 damage, and fortitude reduces it by 1, mitigate would still trigger. Because being immune prevents the damage alltogether, and preventing functions differently than taking it. It&#39;s like with Fright Train and Hippocratic oath; preventing the damage that would be dealt to Fright Train does not cause the first-time-each-turn damage buff to be used up, but reducing it to 0 (like with the environment or something) would.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That&#39;s my interpretation, anyway. Not official by any means.</p>",
